Done. Implementation added to `swift/Sources/NoteKit/NoteKit.swift:18-55`.

**What I added:**
- `NoteParseError` enum with `malformedFormat` case (`Equatable`).
- `parseNote(from:)` — splits on the literal `\n---\n` separator with `omittingEmptySubsequences: false` so empty segments still count, requires exactly 4 parts (else throws), validates the pinned field is `"1"`/`"0"` (else throws), and builds a `Note` reusing `extractTags(from:)` for tags.

**Behavior notes:**
- Wrong part count → `malformedFormat` (no guessing/defaulting).
- Non-`"1"`/`"0"` pinned flag → `malformedFormat`.
- Body tags come from `extractTags(from:)`, so `#tag` tokens in the body populate `tags`; id/title/pinned carry through verbatim.

